// Granted/refreshed by HotFuseSkillAction on dash - empowers Pixie's NEXT Bunny Bomb throw only, not
// a timed buff to every throw for the next few seconds. Remaining ticks down every frame
// (PixieHotFuseTimerSystem, same shape ExplodeOnDeathTimerSystem uses for ExplodeOnDeath.Remaining)
// and the component is removed once it hits zero, so an unused charge "cures" instead of lingering
// forever waiting for a throw that never comes.
//
// Consumed across two points, since damage/instant-detonate need to be locked in at throw time but
// radius is only resolved later, at the bomb's own detonation:
// - ProjectileSkillData.Fire (throw time) - applies DamageMultiplier to this specific throw's damage,
//   and if InstantDetonate is set, grants the existing InstantDetonate tag (see InstantDetonate.qtn)
//   onto the owner so this bomb detonates on first contact instead of waiting out its fuse.
// - AreaHitData.Detonate (this bomb's own detonation, whichever point actually resolves it - hit or
//   planted-fuse expiry) - applies RadiusMultiplier, then removes both this component and the
//   InstantDetonate tag, since both were only ever meant for this one throw.
//
// Only one Bunny Bomb can be in flight from one caster at a time (ProjectileSkillData.Tick blocks a
// re-throw until the current one resolves), so reading/consuming this at Detonate time correctly
// scopes to the throw that consumed it at Fire time in the overwhelming common case - a player
// dashing again mid-flight to refresh the charge before the first bomb lands is a narrow, low-stakes
// edge case, not specifically guarded against.
component PixieHotFuseCharge
{
    FP Remaining;
    FP DamageMultiplier;
    FP RadiusMultiplier;
    Boolean InstantDetonate;
}
